  "releaseNotes": "FastBinary:\n      - Unified all search and comparison operations into a high-performance Generic API with unmanaged constraints.\n      - Eliminated redundant overloads to ensure a lean core engine and prevent method resolution ambiguity.\n      - Optimized the Generic Dispatcher using JIT branch elimination for assembly-level speed on byte and char types.\n      - Resolved a critical recursion issue that caused StackOverflowException during complex span comparisons.\n      Utf8Map and ByteString:\n      - Refactored the internal lookup engine to use a specialized Generic Dispatcher for zero-allocation key matching.\n      - Removed all convenience overloads for char and byte spans to focus strictly on the underlying UTF-8 store.\n      - Enhanced ByteString with a hybrid stack/pool equality logic for efficient char-span comparisons without heap allocation.\n      - Optimized the Freeze() mechanism to transition into a high-speed, read-only state for static routing.\n      - ByteStringComparer now provides consistent, high-performance hashing across all unmanaged key types.",
